/-
A revoke another thread keeps pace with, which breaks "What a holder gave, it takes back" in DESIGN.md.
`before` is the state the seed `revoke-outpaced` reaches as the root's revoke begins, as `host/model.c` wrote it:
a frame of the root's, and two frames derived from it in the second thread's table.
A round is a step of the revoke that stops, then a copy by the second thread of the frame left into the slot the step emptied;
from the state after one round, two more come back to it, so the revoke, made again whenever it stops, never ends,
though `step_forest` makes every state on the way a forest.
It goes once the model follows a remedy of open decision 43.
-/
